     Let me summarize[0m[2m what I found and fixed:
     
     **Bug 1 - Duplicate processing**: In `job_queue.py:dequeue()`, the `await asyncio.sleep(0.01)` yielded[0m[2m control to the event loop after checking `status == "pending"` but before setting `status = "processing"`. This allowed multiple workers to see the same pending job and pick[0m[2m it up. Fix: removed the sleep and added an `asyncio.Lock()` to make the check-and-set atomic[0m[2m.
     
     **Bug 2 - Vanishing failures**: In `worker.py:process_job()`, when an exception was caught, it only printed the error but never called `queue.fail()`. This left[0m[2m jobs stuck in "processing" forever. Fix: added `queue.fail(job["id"], str(e))` to properly record failures.[0m[2m
